&lt;p&gt;• Substantial hands-on experience designing and building evaluation or quality measurement systems for complex technology products, such as search, AI agents, voice technologies, autonomous driving, recommendation systems, advertising, or other similar complex systems..&lt;br&gt;• A track record of owning ambiguous problems from initial framing through implementation, diagnosis, and measurable product improvement..&lt;br&gt;• Strong Python skills and an engineering mindset: you can turn analytical ideas into reliable, maintainable pipelines and tools..&lt;br&gt;• A solid foundation in mathematical statistics and practical experience with experimental design, sampling, uncertainty, and measurement bias..&lt;br&gt;• Strong analytical judgment: you understand what a metric captures, what it misses, and whether an observed improvement matters to users..&lt;br&gt;• The ability to reason across user needs, product behavior, and technical systems, and to translate that understanding into actionable evaluations..&lt;br&gt;• Strong communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to influence technical and product decisions..&lt;br&gt;• The independence to make progress in a fast-moving environment where requirements, methods, and definitions of success are still evolving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
